Z||000003||Cooter||11-26-1999||11:16 PM||||When I put the MSD wires on my 'Burb, I used a little of the left over header wrap around the boots and glued it in place with some high temp red silicone. They have been in place for many trouble free miles, even though they are VERY close to the headers in several places.||||reg||1
Z||000004||DXR_DAD||11-26-1999||11:24 PM||||Tom I have the ACCEL 300+ They are darn good wires, no problems with the heat so far I've had then on about 8 months now.<P>Hay, if you had a deck lid scoop like mine that would get some of that heat out (Smile)! (laugh)! (grin)!||||reg||10
Z||000005||2birds||11-26-1999||11:29 PM||||I have been using Taylor Spiro-Pros, with the straight boots, and no heat shields, for about 5 years and 50,000 miles with no problems on my 86 GT.  They cost me around $32 from Summit, and they are almost impossible to break.  I got mine in red, and it's a perfect match for the engine paint.  They are slightly bigger around than the stock wires but they are a perfect length, IMHO.  ||||reg||1
Z||000006||chris6878||11-26-1999||11:29 PM||||what type of scoop would that be....?||||reg||1
