Z||000019||mwbackus||12-02-1999||07:37 AM||||I use Magnecor KV-85 wires.  Although they are quite expensive, I feel that they are much better than most wires offerered by the high performance market for application on the Fiero when high energy ignition systems are employed.   The jackets can withstand up to 1000° F.  They have a 2.5mm conductor with 200 turn per inch stainless steel windings.  For more information as to why these wires may be superior to others, check the Magnecor site:<P> <A HREF="http://www.magnecor.com/magnecor1/Index.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.magnecor.com/magnecor1/Index.htm</A> <P>P.S.  They are also red, if that matters. :-)<P><BR>Mike<BR>(Fiero info in user profile)||||reg||1
Z||000020||Rob||12-02-1999||07:00 PM|||| I have had the MSD 8.5 wires on my car for about two years now. They have worked just great for me.  ||||reg||14
Z||000021||WKDFIRO||12-03-1999||04:50 AM||||Fiero Motorsports uses Taylor spiropro wires and have never had a problem. Only one that came back was because the back exhaust manifold broke and just cooked that plug wire. We took that boot of in crackly little pieces. No boot could have survived.<P>That was a great picture fierosound! Hope you shortened that coil wire! It looks awfully close to the EGR vavle!||||reg||6
Z||000022||stsmithgt||12-03-1999||09:34 AM||||I've got those 8.5 MDS wires and I put those heatshield tubes on them that came off my old ones.  They seem to be working great.  They didn't give me a color choice and they came in blue.  It looks alright though red looks nicer.||||reg||1
